  "question": "Demonstration: please draw the approximate downward deflection of this cantilever.",
  "reply": "For an Euler–Bernoulli cantilever with a downward tip load F, the static deflection is w(x) = F x^2 (3L - x)/(6EI), taking downward as positive. The orange curve shows the qualitative shape: both deflection and slope are zero at the clamp, and deflection is greatest at the tip. The plotted amplitude is exaggerated for visibility.",
